        "title": "Frankfurt School and Critical Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Frankfurt School (Institut fur Sozialforschung, founded 1923) developed Critical Theory as a synthesis of Marx and Freud -- a method for analyzing how modern capitalist society perpetuates domination. Their media theory, the \"culture industry\" thesis, argues that mass entertainment functions as ideological pacification: it manufactures false needs, forecloses critical consciousness, and produces consent to the existing order."
